<%- include('partials/header') %>
<main id="main-content">
  <section class="page-intro">
    <div class="container">
      <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="/">Home</a></li><li aria-current="page">Solutions</li></ol></nav>
      <p class="eyebrow">Amicus solutions</p>
      <h1>Connectivity for the journey. Coordination for the crew.</h1>
      <p class="lead">Arrange mobile data in the Amicus eSIM store, discuss crew connectivity for your company, or explore the tools that support maritime work.</p>
      <div class="inline-links"><a class="button button-primary" href="<%= site.shopUrl %>" data-event="buy_esim_click">Buy eSIM</a><a href="/operators" class="text-link">Connectivity for your crew</a></div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section" id="connectivity" aria-labelledby="connectivity-heading">
    <div class="container split">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">01 / Amicus eSIM</p><h2 id="connectivity-heading">Mobile data between ship and shore.</h2></div>
      <div class="stack">
        <p>Find eSIM plans for international transit, crew changes, port calls and shore leave. The dedicated Amicus store handles plan selection, prices, coverage, device checks and checkout.</p>
        <p>Check each destination, data allowance and validity before buying. Mobile service depends on the selected plan and local terrestrial networks; it does not replace onboard satellite connectivity.</p>
        <div class="inline-links"><a class="button button-primary" href="<%= site.shopUrl %>" data-event="buy_esim_click">Explore eSIM plans</a><a class="text-link" href="/seafarers">Solutions for seafarers</a></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section section-dark" id="crew-connectivity" aria-labelledby="business-connectivity-heading">
    <div class="container split">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">02 / For companies</p><h2 id="business-connectivity-heading">Prepare joining crew before they leave.</h2></div>
      <div class="stack"><p>Operators, ship managers, manning companies and agents can discuss crew discount-code batches, travel countries and repeat rotations. Agree the arrangement, then give crew a clear purchasing and setup path.</p><p>Company payment or a different distribution process needs confirmation. Describe the workflow your team needs so we can discuss the options.</p><div class="inline-links"><a class="button button-light" href="<%= site.inquiryUrls.connectivity %>" data-event="operator_inquiry">Discuss Crew Connectivity</a><a class="text-link" href="/operators">See the crew workflow</a></div></div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section section-soft" id="operations" aria-labelledby="operations-heading">
    <div class="container split">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">03 / Amicus Crew Change</p><h2 id="operations-heading">Give the journey a shared place.</h2></div>
      <div class="stack"><p>Connect the crew change's vessel and port details, participants, journey stages and messages in one workflow. Learn how the application works and who it is for before registering.</p><p>Local arrangements and responsibilities must still be confirmed with the people handling the operation.</p><div class="inline-links"><a class="button button-secondary" href="<%= site.crewLandingUrl %>">Explore Amicus Crew Change</a><a class="text-link" href="<%= site.inquiryUrls.operations %>" data-event="operator_inquiry">Discuss a crew-change workflow</a></div></div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section" id="tools" aria-labelledby="tools-heading">
    <div class="container split">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">04 / Maritime knowledge</p><h2 id="tools-heading">Prepare for the work ahead.</h2></div>
      <div class="stack"><p>Read maritime guides on connectivity and crew-change travel. The petroleum inspection study tool offers a separate place for question practice.</p><p>Study practice supports preparation; it does not award certification or replace official training, procedures or examination materials.</p><div class="inline-links"><a class="text-link" href="/resources">Browse maritime resources</a><a class="text-link" href="<%= site.inspectionLandingUrl %>">Petroleum inspection study</a></div></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>
<%- include('partials/footer') %>